# Research Strategies

Strategies own research mechanisms, current allocation and next discriminating actions.
Consult the [framework rules](../../framework/rules/strategies.md) and [current hierarchy](index.md).
The exact Task owns its question and authorization; mathematical arguments, results and reviews remain in their responsible materials.

Main Strategies coordinate coherent mechanisms; independently managed Substrategies use the same rolling S type and declare their one current parent in the Route table.
Historical predecessors and current parents have different meanings.
The index derives those relationships and each route's own disposition; it does not assign them.

Find reusable knowledge by the actual conclusion and problem features in Claims, arguments, source audits, related strategies and failed attempts.
Mechanism and lessons sections retain concise guidance with precise evidence; the consuming route explains its own applicability and missing obligations.
Reuse of a completed route does not reopen it, and a parent link supplies neither a proof dependency nor new research authorization.

A local successor may reference a public source route without changing its disposition.
Record its precise source formulation and carried obligations under the [route ownership boundary](../../framework/rules/strategies.md#writable-route-boundary).
Reciprocal updates belong only in locally writable materials; matching authorship does not make a public source writable.

Routine return-link, path and format maintenance in another registered author's local writable S needs no actor change, duplicate feedback, approval or warning log.
Substantive contributions use the responsible human's own numbered materials linked to the original under the [identity rule](../../framework/rules/identity.md).
Tool capability does not authorize substantive cross-author rewriting or takeover of another human's Task/E.
Received originals keep their separate provenance and feedback boundary.
